<title>USA: Watkins-Johnson to divest operations.</title>
<headline>Watkins-Johnson to divest operations.</headline>
<dateline>PALO ALTO, Calif. 1997-04-07</dateline>
<text>
<p>Watkins-Johnson Co said Monday that it is seeking a buyer for its operations which produce defense-electronics components and subassemblies.</p>
<p>In 1996, the operations being divested accounted for over $85 million in revenue.</p>
<p>The company said that although no potential buyers have been identified to date, it expects multiple offers and anticipates that the divestiture will be complete by year-end.</p>
<p>The company plans to retain its product lines aimed at the wireless-infrastructure market.</p>
</text>
